        }
      ],
      "description": "The FLUXNET dataset is a global, community-driven synthesis of measurements from micrometeorological “eddy covariance” towers that quantify the exchanges of carbon dioxide (CO₂), water vapour and energy between terrestrial ecosystems and the atmosphere. At each tower site, high-temporal-resolution measurements of these fluxes and ancillary variables (such as air temperature, precipitation and radiation) are made; these local measurements are then processed, quality-controlled, standardised and aggregated into a consistent global dataset. With more than 1,500 site-years of data from over 200 sites (in the FLUXNET2015 release) and numerous earlier versions (e.g., La Thuile 2007), the dataset spans many ecosystems and climate regimes, enabling biome-to-global scale analyses. The FLUXNET dataset underpins research in ecosystem physiology, carbon cycling, climate-ecosystem feedbacks, and remote sensing validation, and is freely accessible under an open-data policy that emphasises international cooperation and broad scientific reuse.\n\nReference URL: https://fluxnet.org/dat",
      "isReferencedBy": [
        {
          "@type": [
            "dct:BibliographicResource",
            "schema:CreativeWork"
          ],
          "schema:citation": "Pastorello, G., et al. (2020). The FLUXNET2015 dataset and the ONEFlux processing pipeline for eddy covariance data. Scientific Data, 7(1), 225. https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-020-0534-3",
          "identifier": [
            {
              "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
              "propertyID": "DOI",
              "value": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-020-0534-3"
            }
          ],
          "schema:url": [
            "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-020-0534-3"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "reuseExample": [
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Nominator 1:\nGoogle scholar shows 29,000 results with Fluxnet, 12000 for Ameriflux, 3000 for Fluxnet2015."
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Nominator 2:\nIt has been used in hundreds of studies. In the last few years, data from Ameriflux-Fluxnet is cited in at least 100 papers per year."
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Some examples: Understanding how changes in ecosystem management (e.g. Nature-Based Climate Solutions) impact carbon uptake and storage, albedo, evapotranspiration, and other water and energy storage terms (e.g., Zhang et al. 2022, Duman et al. 2021 https://doi.org/10.1016/j.agrformet.2020.108246, Gough et al. 2021 https://doi.org/10.1002/eap.2417, Gough et al, 2022 https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecolind.2022.109004, Arias‐Ortiz et al. 2021 https://doi.org/10.1029/2021JG006573, Yang et al 2024 https://doi.org/10.1016/j.agrformet.2024.110054).",
          "schema:url": [
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.agrformet.2020.108246",
            "https://doi.org/10.1002/eap.2417",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecolind.2022.109004",
            "https://doi.org/10.1029/2021JG006573",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.agrformet.2024.110054"
          ],
          "identifier": [
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.agrformet.2020.108246",
            "https://doi.org/10.1002/eap.2417",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecolind.2022.109004",
            "https://doi.org/10.1029/2021JG006573",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.agrformet.2024.110054"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Diagnosing the impacts of natural disturbances like fire, heat waves, droughts, and insect outbreaks (e.g., Rastogi et al. 2022 https://doi.org/10.1029/2022GL097959).",
          "schema:url": [
            "https://doi.org/10.1029/2022GL097959"
          ],
          "identifier": [
            "https://doi.org/10.1029/2022GL097959"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Exploring how topographic gradients in temperature and water availability impact ecosystem productivity and hydrologic cycling (e.g., Shveyster et al., 2024 https://doi.org/10.1029/2022WR033757)",
          "schema:url": [
            "https://doi.org/10.1029/2022WR033757"
          ],
          "identifier": [
            "https://doi.org/10.1029/2022WR033757"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Understanding how spatial heterogeneity and land-atmosphere coupling impacts a wide range of boundary-layer processes (e.g. Butterworth et al 2021 https://doi.org/10.1175/BAMS-D-19-0346.1, Butterworth et al 2024 https://doi.org/10.3389/feart.2023.1251138; Wanner et al., 2024 https://doi.org/10.1007/s10546-024-00868-8).",
          "schema:url": [
            "https://doi.org/10.1175/BAMS-D-19-0346.1",
            "https://doi.org/10.3389/feart.2023.1251138",
            "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10546-024-00868-8"
          ],
          "identifier": [
            "https://doi.org/10.1175/BAMS-D-19-0346.1",
            "https://doi.org/10.3389/feart.2023.1251138",
            "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10546-024-00868-8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Scaling to regions, including quantifying lateral fluxes, terrestrial-aquatic linkages, and other carbon transfers required for full carbon accounting and model-data and top down-bottom-up comparison (e.g., Metzger et al., 2021 https://doi.org/10.5194/amt-14-6929-2021, Zhang et a; 2023 https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.14188)",
          "schema:url": [
            "https://doi.org/10.5194/amt-14-6929-2021",
            "https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.14188"
          ],
          "identifier": [
            "https://doi.org/10.5194/amt-14-6929-2021",
            "https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.14188"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
