      "description": "See https://disc.gsfc.nasa.gov/datasets/GPM_3IMERGHH_07/summary?keywords=IMERG\n\nIMERG is NASA’s open-source observational global precipitation product. It is the unified U.S. GPM algorithm that provides precipitation products at half-hour 0.1°x0.1° globally for 1998-present. The estimates from the available precipitation-relevant satellite passive microwave (PMW) sensors are computed, intercalibrated, and merged. Merged geo-IR estimates are computed, intercalibrated to the PMW, and input to a Morphing-Kalman Filter along with the PMW. Motion vectors for the quasi-Lagrangian PMW morphing are computed from numerical reanalysis (Final) and numerical forecast (Early and Late) data fields. \n\nThe IMERG system is run twice in near-real time:\n• \"Early\" multi-satellite product ~4 hr after observation (forward morphing only) and\n• \"Late\" multi-satellite product ~14 hr after observation (forward and backward morphing),\nand once after real time:\n• \"Final\", satellite-gauge product ~4 months after the observation month, (forward and backward morphing, monthly gauge analyses).\n\nEach new version of IMERG reprocesses the entire 1998–present record for all three Runs to ensure consistency regardless of which Run a user employs. Moreover, NASA produces value-added products that answer user needs, such as daily accumulations, GeoTIFF formats, and on-demand parameter and geographical subsetting. Data fields include the complete precipitation field, Quality Index, and Probability of Liquid Precipitation.",
      "isReferencedBy": [
