    {
      "@id": "id:dataset:014",
      "@type": [
        "dcat:Dataset",
        "schema:Dataset"
      ],
      "title": "PARMA/EXPACS",
      "wasDerivedFrom": "id:sourcerow:014",
      "theme": [
        "id:theme:atmospheric-science-space-weather"
      ],
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "agu:CreatorStatement",
          "name": "Tatsuhiko Sato"
        }
      ],
      "landingPage": [
        "https://phits.jaea.go.jp/expacs/index.html"
      ],
      "inCatalog": [
        "id:repository:japan-atomic-energy-agency"
      ],
      "description": "PARMA/EXPACS is a globally applicable dataset and calculator of atmospheric cosmic-ray particle spectra and radiation dose fields, available free of charge from Japan Atomic Energy Agency. Built on the PHITS-based Analytical Radiation Model in the Atmosphere (PARMA), EXPACS rapidly returns location-, altitude-, date- and solar-cycle-dependent fluxes of neutrons, protons, heavy ions (Z≤28), muons, electrons/positrons and photons, together with derived quantities such as effective dose, ambient dose equivalent, absorbed dose in air and ion-pair production rates. The underlying model has been extensively validated against measurements over a wide range of geomagnetic cutoffs, altitudes and solar conditions, and successive PARMA releases widened the physics coverage (e.g., zenith-angle dependence) and application domains. Because EXPACS is Excel-based with well-documented inputs/outputs, it lowers the barrier to reproducible analyses for researchers and practitioners across disciplines. The dataset underpins operational aviation dose assessment, public exposure evaluation, geoscience applications (cosmogenic nuclide scaling), near-surface hydrology (cosmic-ray neutron sensing), muon radiography and semiconductor soft-error studies, making it a cross-cutting community resource rather than a niche tool.",
