          ]
        }
      ],
      "reuseExample": [
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Links to other reusers are:"
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "The Global Burden of Disease Project www.healthdata.org/research-analysis/gbd\nThe World Health Organization www.who.int/health-topics/air-pollution\nThe Air Quality Life Index aqli.epic.uchicago.edu/\nThe OECD Regional Well-Being Index www.oecdregionalwellbeing.org/\nThe HEI State of Global Air www.stateofglobalair.org/\nThe Environmental Performance Index epi.yale.edu/\nThe World Bank Sustainable Development Goal tracking prosperitydata360.worldbank.org/en/indicator/\nThe American Lung Association www.lung.org/research/sota"
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "The Integrated Science Assessment (EPA 2019) and its Supplement (EPA 2022) that underpin the updated EPA PM2.5 standard collectively include over 100 citations describing and applying these satellite-derived PM2.5 data. The final rule itself (89 FR 16202) also includes multiple references to these satellite-derived PM2.5 data and its applications."
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "EPA, U. (2019). Integrated Science Assessment (ISA) for Particulate Matter (Final Report, Dec 2019): U.S. Environmental Protection Agency, Washington, DC, EPA/600/R-619/188, 2019."
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "EPA, U. S. (2022). Supplement to the 2019 Integrated Science Assessment for Particulate Matter (Final Report, 2022): U.S. Environmental Protection Agency, Washington, DC, EPA/635/R-622/028, 2022."
