        {
          "@type": "agu:CuratorStatement",
          "name": "Brigitte Stoll"
        }
      ],
      "description": "GeoReM is a database for reference materials of geological and environmental interest, such as rock powders, synthetic and natural glasses as well as mineral, isotopic, biological, river and seawater reference materials. GeoReM contains published analytical data and compilation values (major and trace element concentrations and mass fractions, radiogenic and stale isotope ratios). GeoReM contains all important metadata about the analytical values such as uncertainty, analytical method and laboratory. Sample information and references are also included.\nGeoReM contains about 67,500 analyses of more than 4,100 RM from about 13,900 peer-reviewed publications, certified values of 718 RM and preferred analytical values for 61 RM. GeoReM was accessed more than 34,000 times with 1000 downloads by researchers from 117 countries with most from China, USA, Germany, UK, France and Canada.\nEffective September 11, 2025, the rights to GeoReM and the associated responsibilities have been transferred from the Max Planck Institute for Chemistry in Mainz to the International Association of Geoanalysts (IAG), represented by IAGeo Limited (https://www.geoanalyst.org/). At the time of submission, the database and IT-related peripherals will be transferred to the DFG-funded DIGIS 2.0 project at the University of Göttingen, which will ensure a secure IT structure and curation of the database in collaboration with the IAG. The contact person for this process is Axel Renno (a.renno@hzdr.de).",
