          "sourceColumn": "Short description (1500 characters) of the dataset being nominated. ",
          "schema:value": "The International GNSS Service serves as the premier source of the highest-quality GNSS related standards and conventions, data and products\".\n\nAll IGS data and products are openly available to all user communities, free of charge.\n\n\"The IGS collects, archives, and distributes high-quality GNSS observational data\nsets to satisfy the objectives of a wide range of scientific and other high-end\napplications and experimentation. These data sets are used by the IGS to\ngenerate the following data products:\n ● High accuracy GNSS satellite ephemerides and related information\n ● Earth rotation parameters\n ● Coordinates and velocities of the IGS tracking stations\n ● GNSS satellite and tracking station clock information, timescale products\n ● Ionospheric information\n ● Tropospheric information\"\n\nThe core IGS Data and Products are generated by \"operational components\" and global and regional data and analysis centers. \nThe components are coordinated by the IGS Central Bureau and IGS Governing Board, and various global and regional data repositories store raw data and products produced by different components. One of the global repositories is managed by NASA's Crustal Dynamics Data and Information System (CDDIS), and distributes all IGS data and products via https://files.igs.org/ . \n\nThe quoted part of this description is copied from the IGS Terms of Reference (https://files.igs.org/pub/resource/governance/IGS-Terms-of-Reference-2023.pdf), that provides a detailed overview of IGS components and governance."
