        },
        {
          "sourceColumn": "Short description (1500 characters) of the dataset being nominated. ",
          "schema:value": "OCTOPUS is an open, web-based geochronological database that makes published Quaternary and landscape-evolution data easier to find, query, visualise and reuse. It brings together cosmogenic radionuclide measurements, especially Be-10 and Al-26, luminescence ages, radiocarbon ages and denudation-rate data from studies of erosional landscapes, fluvial basins, glacial landforms, depositional environments, palaeoenvironmental archives and archaeological records.\n\nThe database is compliant with Open Geospatial Consortium standards, so its data can be accessed through the OCTOPUS web interface and compatible desktop GIS software. In addition to analytical results, OCTOPUS stores metadata such as bibliographic details, sample context, preparation and measurement information, and associated geospatial layers. For cosmogenic-nuclide denudation datasets, it also provides information and input files required to recalculate basin-wide denudation rates using published code and web-enabled calculators.\n\nThis makes OCTOPUS more than a simple data catalogue: it is a curated infrastructure for reanalysing legacy datasets, comparing records across regions, testing geomorphic and palaeoenvironmental hypotheses, and improving transparency and reproducibility in geochronology. It follows FAIR principles, aiming to make geochronological data findable, accessible, interoperable and reusable for researchers, students, landform modellers and others working across Earth-surface processes, Quaternary science and archaeology."
        },
        {
          "sourceColumn": "Justification for inclusion in AGU commentary. Why is the nominated dataset impactful “in your own words” or “in your opinion”.\nPeople: education, training, disaster response and prediction\nPlanet: geophysical phenomena, conservation, climate, environmental indicators\nProsperity: economic good, social equity, humanitarian relief, community resilience",
          "schema:value": "OCTOPUS has set a new benchmark for Indigenous data governance in Australia by integrating both the FAIR (Findability, Accessibility, Interoperability, and Reusability) and CARE (Collective Benefit, Authority to Control, Responsibility, and Ethics) principles. As a globally registered data repository, OCTOPUS supports a broad international user community and has fulfilled over 3,500 individual data requests from researchers worldwide. The platform is widely employed in research, postgraduate training, and university teaching across multiple countries. Its extensive datasets have enabled global and regional geomorphological studies that were previously unattainable, providing a foundation for testing key hypotheses in Earth surface processes. Moreover, OCTOPUS has significantly advanced recent models of the initial peopling of the Australian continent."
        },
        {
          "sourceColumn": "Short description of how you interact with this dataset.  ",
          "schema:value": "The nominator is the creator and lead maintainer of this database."
        },
        {
          "sourceColumn": "Reference publication that describes the dataset.",
          "schema:value": "Codilean, A. T., & Munack, H. (2025). Short communication: Updated CRN Denudation collections in OCTOPUS v2.3. Geochronology, 7(1), 113–122. https://doi.org/10.5194/gchron-7-113-2025 \n\nHerbert, A. V., Haberle, S. G., Munack, H., & Codilean, A. T. (2025). Collaborative effort towards a fair and open indo-pacific pollen database(Ippd). Data Science Journal, 24, 5. https://doi.org/10.5334/dsj-2025-005 \n\nRehn, E., et al. (2025). The sahulchar collection: A palaeofire database for australia, new guinea, and new zealand. Earth System Science Data, 17(6), 2681–2692. https://doi.org/10.5194/essd-17-2681-2025 \n\nSaktura, W. M., et al. (2023). SahulArch: A geochronological database for the archaeology of Sahul. Australian Archaeology, 89(1), 1–13. https://doi.org/10.1080/03122417.2022.2159751 \n\nCodilean, A. T., et al. (2022). OCTOPUS database (V. 2). Earth System Science Data, 14(8), 3695–3713. https://doi.org/10.5194/essd-14-3695-2022 \n\nCodilean, A. T., Munack, H., Cohen, T. J., Saktura, W. M., Gray, A., & Mudd, S. M. (2018). OCTOPUS: An open cosmogenic isotope and luminescence database. Earth System Science Data, 10(4), 2123–2139. https://doi.org/10.5194/essd-10-2123-2018"
