        {
          "sourceColumn": "Examples of how this dataset has been reused, any bibliographies listing instances of reuse, or any references to derived data products/datasets. ",
          "schema:value": "This is an incomplete list of publications using the OCTOPUS database for regional or global scale analyses:\n\nChen, Y., Wu, B., Xiong, Z., Zan, J., Zhang, B., Zhang, R., Xue, Y., Li, M., & Li, B. (2021). Evolution of eastern Tibetan river systems is driven by the indentation of India. Communications Earth & Environment, 2(1), 256. https://doi.org/10.1038/s43247-021-00330-4 \n\nHalsted, C., Bierman, P., Codilean, A., Corbett, L., and Caffee, M. (2024). Global analysis of in situ cosmogenic 26Al/10Be ratios in fluvial sediments indicates widespread sediment storage and burial during transport. Geochronology Discuss. [preprint], https://doi.org/10.5194/gchron-2024-22, in review.\n\nWilner, J. A., Nordin, B. J., Getraer, A., Gregoire, R. M., Krishna, M., Li, J., Pickell, D. J., Rogers, E. R., McDannell, K. T., Palucis, M. C., & Keller, C. (2024). Limits to timescale dependence in erosion rates: Quantifying glacial and fluvial erosion across timescales. Science Advances, 10(51), eadr2009. https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.adr2009 \n\nZondervan, J. R., Hilton, R. G., Dellinger, M., Clubb, F. J., Roylands, T., & Ogrič, M. (2023). Rock organic carbon oxidation CO2 release offsets silicate weathering sink. Nature, 623(7986), 329–333. https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06581-9 \n\nGodard, V., & Tucker, G. E. (2021). Influence of climate‐forcing frequency on hillslope response. Geophysical Research Letters, 48(18), e2021GL094305. https://doi.org/10.1029/2021GL094305 \n\nDelunel, R., Schlunegger, F., Valla, P. G., Dixon, J., Glotzbach, C., Hippe, K., Kober, F., Molliex, S., Norton, K. P., Salcher, B., Wittmann, H., Akçar, N., & Christl, M. (2020). Late-Pleistocene catchment-wide denudation patterns across the European Alps. Earth-Science Reviews, 211, 103407. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.earscirev.2020.103407 \n\nWhipple, K., Adams, B., Forte, A., & Hodges, K. (2023). Eroding the himalaya: Topographic and climatic control of erosion rates and implications for tectonics. The Journal of Geology, 131(4), 265–288. https://doi.org/10.1086/731260 \n\nCrabtree, S. A., White, D. A., Bradshaw, C. J. A., Saltré, F., Williams, A. N., Beaman, R. J., Bird, M. I., & Ulm, S. (2021). Landscape rules predict optimal superhighways for the first peopling of Sahul. Nature Human Behaviour, 5(10), 1303–1313. https://doi.org/10.1038/s41562-021-01106-8 \n\nBradshaw, et al. (2021). Stochastic models support rapid peopling of Late Pleistocene Sahul. Nature Communications, 12(1), 2440. https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-021-21551-3 \n\nCodilean, A. T., Fülöp, R.-H., Munack, H., Wilcken, K. M., Cohen, T. J., Rood, D. H., Fink, D., Bartley, R., Croke, J., & Fifield, L. K. (2021). Controls on denudation along the East Australian continental margin. Earth-Science Reviews, 214, 103543. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.earscirev.2021.103543 \n\nFülöp, R.-H., et al. (2020). Million-year lag times in a post-orogenic sediment conveyor. Science Advances, 6(25), eaaz8845. https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.aaz8845"
