structions focused only on tropical cyclone activity currently exist. It has also been noted that using the sedimentary record to examine extreme weather events of short duration is complex and thus requires clear comprehension of the natural processes involved, which was a major motivation for this dataset.\n\nHence, the diatoms included in this dataset can be used as environmental indicators to examine geophysical phenomena such as tropical cyclones and the impact they have on physical systems such as anchialine aquifers. They can also further be used as paleoenvironmental indicators to examine past hydrological changes and tropical cyclone activity, which may yield important insights into freshwater management of coastal aquifers in today’s changing climate as well as provide a comparable historical analogue for future projections of tropical cyclone activity. To this point, the diatoms included in this dataset can thus also be utilized as environmental indicators to aid in disaster prediction of future tropical cyclones."
