    {
      "@id": "id:dataset:095",
      "@type": [
        "dcat:Dataset",
        "schema:Dataset"
      ],
      "title": "ITS_LIVE Global Ice Velocity",
      "wasDerivedFrom": "id:sourcerow:095",
      "theme": [
        "id:theme:ocean-science-hydrology-cryosphere"
      ],
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "agu:CreatorStatement",
          "name": "Alex Gardner, Joe Kennedy, Maria Liukis, Mark Fahnestock, Chad Greene, Luis Lòpez, Ted Scambos"
        }
      ],
      "landingPage": [
        "https://its-live.jpl.nasa.gov"
      ],
      "inCatalog": [
        "id:repository:jet-propulsion-laboratory-and-national-snow-and-ice-data-center"
      ],
      "curator": [
        {
          "@type": "agu:CuratorStatement",
          "name": "Joe Kennedy, Maria Liukis, Luis Lòpez"
        }
      ],
      "description": "ITS_LIVE is a global, multi-satellite, near-real-time compilation of ice velocity data for all of Earth's ice areas larger than 5 km^2. The data coverage begins in 1984 with Landsat 4 and continues up to the present, incorporating Landsat 5, 7, 8 and 9, Sentinel 1 and 2, and (planned) NISAR image pairs for ice mapping. Derived products include annual mosaic compilations of major ice regions, ice edge extent maps for Greenland tidewater glaciers and Antarctica's ice shelves, and data cubes of the available image pair data for tiled areas of the globe. \n\nThe data is served from the AWS cloud, and is also available for browse and download through an interactive website that permits time-series data download for any location in the archive [https://its-live.jpl.nasa.gov/app/index.html].\n\nThe data set, in existence since 2019, has now supported dozens of studies of glacier and ice sheet processes, mass balance, and seasonal ice flux variations. The comprehensiveness and ease of access make ITS_LIVE an exceptional global change dataset for science or for education.",
