          "schema:value": "As a PhD student, the nominator has been directly involved in the collection of MarineBasis data in Young Sound for the past two years, gaining first-hand experience in Arctic fieldwork and the stewardship of long-term datasets. Their connection to GEM began earlier, during their Master’s studies, when they used GEM data in courses to understand Arctic coastal ecosystems and how they respond to a changing climate. Since then, MarineBasis has been integral to their research: they have published two articles in their PhD that relied on GEM data, both as a foundation for analyses and as essential context for experimental studies conducted in the same environment. Even when their work does not directly analyze MarineBasis measurements, the ancillary data (e.g., hydrography, nutrient concentrations, sea ice conditions) provide invaluable context, enabling more robust interpretation of results. Beyond publications, GEM has shaped their training and growth as an Arctic researcher, serving as both a scientific resource and a learning platform."
        },
