        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "DOI",
          "value": "https://doi.org/10.5067/SWTPO-MOOR2"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "DOI",
          "value": "https://doi.org/10.5067/SWTPO-MOOR3"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "DOI",
          "value": "https://doi.org/10.5067/SWTPO-GLDR1"
        }
      ],
      "inCatalog": [
        "id:repository:po-daac"
      ],
      "description": "In 2023, 11 moorings and two gliders were deployed off California as part of calibration/validation (cal/val) efforts for the SWOT satellite mission. SWOT (Surface Water and Ocean Topography) is a satellite mission that measures sea surface height with a radar altimeter. In this dataset collection, temperature and salinity data from the moorings and gliders are reported. The mooring sensors were on profiling instruments in the upper 500 m, and from additional instruments fixed on the mooring wire below 500 m. Different processing levels of the mooring data are available, including easy-to-use gridded data versions that merge data from multiple instruments/moorings on a common set of vertical and time coordinates. Other data versions, such as gridded data from individual moorings with somewhat finer resolution, as well as the underlying non-gridded data records at their original instrumental resolution, are available separately. Glider data as well as ship-based data that were used to calibrate the mooring data are available separately. One of the moorings was maintained for a year beyond the SWOT cal/val phase as part of a project that studies internal waves; these data are included in the collection as well.",
      "isReferencedBy": [
        {
          "@type": [
            "dct:BibliographicResource",
            "schema:CreativeWork"
          ],
          "schema:citation": "Wang, J., Lucas, A. J., Stalin, S., Lankhorst, M., Send, U., Schofield, O., Kachelein, L., Haines, B., Meinig, C., Pinkel, R., Farrar, J. T., & Fu, L. (2025). Swot mission validation of sea surface height measurements at sub‐100 km scales. Geophysical Research Letters, 52(11), e2025GL114936. https://doi.org/10.1029/2025GL114936",
          "identifier": [
            {
              "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
              "propertyID": "DOI",
              "value": "https://doi.org/10.1029/2025GL114936"
            }
          ],
          "schema:url": [
            "https://doi.org/10.1029/2025GL114936"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4166-4044",
      "@type": [
        "schema:Person",
