        {
          "sourceColumn": "Short description (1500 characters) of the dataset being nominated. ",
          "schema:value": "EStreams is a comprehensive dataset that includes streamflow indices, catchment-aggregated hydro-climatic signatures, and landscape attributes (such as topography, soils, geology, vegetation, and land cover) across Europe. Covering 17,130 catchments from 41 countries and spanning up to 120 years, it represents the largest online resource of its kind. Beyond being a dataset, EStreams also serves as a catalogue, offering detailed metadata that enables users to directly access original streamflow data sources. This design helps overcome challenges related to data redistribution policies, language differences, and the diversity of national data portals. Designed to be dynamic rather than static, EStreams can be readily updated to include new stations or more recent data. It includes Python scripts for data retrieval, aggregation, processing, and updates, allowing users to seamlessly integrate newly available or revised streamflow records. EStreams facilitates continental-scale hydrological modelling, climate impact assessments, and large-sample, reproducible hydrological research. Since its launch, it has proven to be an invaluable resource for numerous scientific projects across Europe."
        },
        {
