    {
      "@id": "id:dataset:125",
      "@type": [
        "dcat:Dataset",
        "schema:Dataset"
      ],
      "title": "Geospace Regions and Magnetospheric Boundaries (GRMB) identification dataset",
      "wasDerivedFrom": "id:sourcerow:125",
      "theme": [
        "id:theme:space-and-planetary-science"
      ],
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "agu:CreatorStatement",
          "name": "Benjamin Grison, Institute of Atmospheric Physics, Czech Academy of Science, Czechia, grison@ufa.cas.cz"
        }
      ],
      "landingPage": [
        "https://doi.org/10.57780/esa-85c563c"
      ],
      "identifier": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "DOI",
          "value": "https://doi.org/10.57780/esa-85c563c"
        }
      ],
      "inCatalog": [
        "id:repository:european-space-agency"
      ],
      "curator": [
        {
          "@type": "agu:CuratorStatement",
          "name": "Arnaud Masson"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The Geospace Region and Magnetospheric Boundary identification (GRMB) dataset contains the label of the region in which the Cluster satellites are travelling. It results from visual selection of the boundary in pregenerated plots given by ESA/CSA. Each record indicates the time interval passed in a GRMB region (the exit time of this region is the next entry time). The label is described as a string and as number (1 to 15): \n1. IN/UKN: Inside the magnetosphere; 2. IN/PLS: Plasmasphere; 3. IN/PPTR: Plasmapause Transition Region; 4. IN/PSH: Plasmasheet; 5. IN/PSTR: Plasmasheet Transition Region; 6. IN/LOB: Lobe; 7. IN/POL: Polar Regions; 8. IN/MP: Magnetopause; 9. IN/MPTR: Magnetopause Transition Region; 10. OUT/MSH: Magnetosheath; 11. OUT/BSTR: Bow Shock Transition Region; 12. OUT/SWF: Solar Wind and Foreshock; 13. OUT/UKN: Outside the magnetosphere; 14. UNKNOWN: Available data are not conclusive; 15. N/A: No data.\nSince this information has been generated by visual inspection of existing plots (with a pixel resolution down to 7s), the change of a region is not resolved with a constant time resolution. \nSee the user guide for more informations: Grison, B. et al. Localization of the Cluster satellites in the geospace environment. Sci Data 12, 327 (2025). https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-025-04639-z \nThe GRMB project is a cooperation between the Institute of Atmospheric Physics of the Czech Academy of Science and the Royal Belgian Institute for Space Aeronomy.",
      "isReferencedBy": [
        {
          "@type": [
            "dct:BibliographicResource",
            "schema:CreativeWork"
          ],
          "schema:citation": "Grison, B., et al. (2025). Localization of the Cluster satellites in the geospace environment. Scientific Data, 12(1), 327. https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-025-04639-z",
          "identifier": [
            {
              "@type": "schema:PropertyValue",
              "propertyID": "DOI",
              "value": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-025-04639-z"
            }
          ],
          "schema:url": [
            "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-025-04639-z"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "reuseExample": [
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Grimmich, N., et al. (2024). The Cluster spacecrafts’ view of the motion of the high-latitude magnetopause. Annales Geophysicae, 42(2), 371–394. https://doi.org/10.5194/angeo-42-371-2024",
          "schema:url": [
            "https://doi.org/10.5194/angeo-42-371-2024"
          ],
          "identifier": [
