      "reuseExample": [
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Nominator 1:\nhttps://www.nature.com/articles/495300a",
          "schema:url": [
            "https://www.nature.com/articles/495300a"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Nominator 2:\nRoughly 1700 publications at https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/search/fq=%7B!type%3Daqp%20v%3D%24fq_database%7D&fq_database=(database%3Aastronomy%20OR%20database%3Aphysics)&p_=0&q=%20full%3A%22silso%22%20year%3A2013-&sort=date%20desc%2C%20bibcode%20desc",
          "schema:url": [
            "https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/search/fq=%7B!type%3Daqp%20v%3D%24fq_database%7D&fq_database=(database%3Aastronomy%20OR%20database%3Aphysics"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Nominator 3:\nThis dataset is reused in many different contexts from Space Weather (e.g. forecasting solar wind speed:https://doi.org/10.3847/1538-4365/adf436) to Climate research (e.g. ENSO climate variability: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jastp.2025.106490) to marine biology (e.g. flowering of seagrass: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecss.2025.109483) or technical maintenance of satellites or measurements (e.g. F10.7 :https://doi.org/10.1029/2024SW004060). And this is just a few examples, the Sunspot Number is used in many different fields including the stock markets (e.g. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.techfore.2007.07.001).",
          "schema:url": [
            "https://doi.org/10.3847/1538-4365/adf436",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jastp.2025.106490",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecss.2025.109483",
            "https://doi.org/10.1029/2024SW004060",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.techfore.2007.07.001"
          ],
          "identifier": [
            "https://doi.org/10.3847/1538-4365/adf436",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jastp.2025.106490",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecss.2025.109483",
            "https://doi.org/10.1029/2024SW004060",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.techfore.2007.07.001"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Nominator 4:\nThis dataset is reused in many different contexts from Space Weather (e.g. forecasting solar wind speed :https://doi.org/10.3847/1538-4365/adf436) to Climate research (e.g. ENSO climate variability : https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jastp.2025.106490) to marine biology (e.g. flowering of seagrass : https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecss.2025.109483) or technical maintenance of satellites or measurements (e.g. F10.7 :https://doi.org/10.1029/2024SW004060). And this is just a few examples, the Sunspot Number is used in many different fields including the stock markets (e.g. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.techfore.2007.07.001).",
          "schema:url": [
            "https://doi.org/10.3847/1538-4365/adf436",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jastp.2025.106490",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecss.2025.109483",
            "https://doi.org/10.1029/2024SW004060",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.techfore.2007.07.001"
          ],
          "identifier": [
            "https://doi.org/10.3847/1538-4365/adf436",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jastp.2025.106490",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecss.2025.109483",
            "https://doi.org/10.1029/2024SW004060",
            "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.techfore.2007.07.001"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Nominator 5: \nThe Sunspot Number is one of the most widely used datasets in the geosciences and space sciences. It serves as a fundamental reference for studies on solar activity, heliophysics, space weather, and Sun–Earth interactions, as well as for research in climate science and long-term variability of the Earth’s atmosphere."
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Evidence of its extensive reuse can be found in the vast number of scientific papers that reference or rely on it. For example, a search on the SciX platform (https://scixplorer.org/search?n=10&p=1&q=abs%3A%22Sunspot+Number%22&sort=score+desc&sort=date+desc\n) for publications containing “Sunspot Number” in the abstract returns hundreds of records, revealing continuous scientific interest in this dataset for more than a century.",
          "schema:url": [
            "https://scixplorer.org/search?n=10&p=1&q=abs%3A%22Sunspot+Number%22&sort=score+desc&sort=date+desc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "Furthermore, the citation record of the main papers describing the dataset highlights its exceptional impact. The key reference, Clette et al. (2014, Space Science Reviews), currently has 542 citations in SciX and 822 in Google Scholar (as of 9 October 2025), confirming the dataset’s central role in solar and geophysical research."
        },
        {
          "@type": "agu:ReuseExample",
          "schema:text": "The Sunspot Number has also inspired a number of derived products and complementary datasets, such as sunspot catalogs, group sunspot numbers, and reconstructed solar activity indices. These derivatives, together with the International Sunspot Number Version 2.0, form the backbone of solar activity reconstructions spanning the past four centuries and are essential for multidisciplinary studies linking solar variability with terrestrial and planetary processes."
        }
      ]
    },
